WEBVTT

1
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.000
Nathan B.: Let's start with the self-serve tier. Smith looked at the market for us.

2
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:50.000
Smith: I did. Five competitors, and every one of them prices per practitioner.

3
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:13.000
Nathan B.: Our $49 floor blocks single-practitioner clinics. I'd add a $19 entry tier with a 60-day trial.

4
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Emma C.: Sixty days is long. Why not thirty?

5
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.000
Nathan B.: Clinics need two billing cycles to see the reminders pay off.

6
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:49.000
Smith: Competitors anchor at $25 to $29, so $19 reads as an entry offer, not a discount.

7
00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:58.000
Nathan B.: The page still says $49 everywhere.

8
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Emma C.: And the copy is written for multi-site groups.

9
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Emma C.: Then we need to rewrite pricing for self-serve by Friday.

10
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.000
Nathan B.: Friday is tight, but fine.

11
00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.000
Emma C.: Daniel can help with the layout.

12
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:56.000
Emma C.: Do we have to launch it before the campaign? We could wait until November.

13
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:20.000
Smith: A price change right after the ads go out confuses people.

14
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Nathan B.: The creative already assumes $19. We can't move it.

15
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Emma C.: Agreed. We ship the $19 tier before the Q4 campaign.

16
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
Smith: That's the right call.

17
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.000
Nathan B.: Good. Next, the copy work.

18
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.000
Nathan B.: Do we have a ticket for the pricing changes?

19
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.000
Emma C.: Let me check.

20
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Emma C.: Wait, this is basically the pricing ticket we already have.

21
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:19.000
Nathan B.: GRW-180? Then put the Friday deadline on it.

22
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Emma C.: Will do. The copy rewrite gets its own ticket.

23
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.000
Nathan B.: Last big item: existing customers.

24
00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Emma C.: You mean the annual plans?

25
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:27.000
Nathan B.: Existing annual plans are the open risk; no customer should pay more after the change. If the pricing copy freezes Friday, engineering can cut the release on Monday.

26
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
Emma C.: Copy freezes Friday. Deal.

27
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Nathan B.: I'll keep an eye on the annual-plan migration until the release branch is cut.

28
00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.000
Smith: Grandfathering them for a year is the norm.

29
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:08.000
Emma C.: Let's not promise a year yet.

30
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:34.000
Emma C.: Smith, what do clinics compare when they shop?

31
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:54.000
Smith: I asked a dozen clinic owners last month.

32
00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:18.000
Smith: Clinics compare per-practitioner price, not per-site. I'd lead the page with that unit.

33
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:26.000
Emma C.: So the page leads with the price per practitioner.

34
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:35.000
Nathan B.: Unit first, then the trial.

35
00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:13.000
Nathan B.: What about clinics that left us?

36
00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:33.000
Smith: Win-back offers usually leave out recent churn.

37
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:56.000
Emma C.: Does the 60-day trial apply to clinics that churned in the last year?

38
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.000
Nathan B.: Good question. I don't know.

39
00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:12.000
Emma C.: Let's park it.

40
00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:29.000
Smith: Watch the annual wording. Refund terms trip people up.

41
00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:54.000
Emma C.: I'm not comfortable writing that part myself.

42
00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:16.000
Nathan B.: Okay, let's get legal to look at the annual wording before it goes live.

43
00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:26.000
Emma C.: Good. I'll leave annual out of Friday's copy.

44
00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:38.000
Nathan B.: Thanks, Smith. That's it for today.
